* New enemies
- Helion
- Burrowed banelings
- Something that becomes terrain when dying or when doing something else (supply depo), could soak up projectiles
- Viper pull
- Pushing away the players when dying or pulling them in
- Stealth

* Scoreboard: Save Game Progress locally
- localStorage & sessionStorage: Store high scores, unlocked levels, player inventories, and save states. When your friend closes the browser and reopens the HTML file tomorrow, their progress will still be there.
- JSON Import/Export: Add a simple "Export Save" button that copies a text code to their clipboard so they can send their save data back to you.

* Embed All Visual & Audio Assets Locally
- You don't need external .png or .mp3 files lying around in a folder next to your HTML.
Base64 Data URIs: You can encode images, audio clips, and fonts into text strings directly in your CSS or JavaScript (data:image/png;base64,...).
- Procedural Graphics: Use the HTML5 <canvas> API or WebGL/GLSL to draw shapes, particle systems, and visual effects in real time using math instead of heavy image files.
- Web Audio API: Synthesize sound effects (jump sounds, explosions, retro chiptune bleeps) on the fly using code oscillators, zero audio files required.


FUTURE IDEAS
* Make the environment change

* Random upgrades to the opponents?
- Armor
- Movement speed

* Advanced Engine Tech & 3D
- Inline JS Libraries: You can bundle full libraries (like Three.js, Phaser, or Matter.js physics) directly into your <script> tag by pasting their minified source code.
- WebAssembly (Wasm): Encode compiled C/C++ or Rust code as a Base64 string to run high-performance logic directly in the browser.